Tips Learned
 Use long passwords or passphrases (at least 16 characters).
 Include mixed character types.
 Make passwords unique per account.
 Avoid common words and predictable patterns.
 Use password managers.
 Understand attacks to appreciate password complexity’s role in defense.
   
